prevent future void by reduce costs and set reminders.

.why = now that you're restored, take steps to avoid this situation again.

---

## reduce franchise tax (optional but recommended)

if you have ≤5,000 issued shares, you can reduce authorized shares to pay $175/year instead of $400/year.

| authorized shares | annual tax |
|-------------------|------------|
| 10,000,000 | **$400 floor** (Assumed Par Value) — ⚠️ rises with gross assets, see below |
| 5,000 | **$175 flat** (Authorized Shares Method) — assets do not enter it |

> 🚩 **the first row read a flat `$400` until 2026-09-02.** $400 is the
> § 503(a)(2) **minimum**, not the rate. measured at 10,000,000 authorized /
> 8,000,000 issued:
>
> | gross assets | annual tax |
> |---|---:|
> | $50 · $500,000 | $400.00 |
> | $5,000,000 | **$2,800.00** |
>
> ⭐ **and note which way this one cuts.** an understated *before* column makes
> the reduction look **less** worth doing, not more. a corp at $5M assets is
> told it saves $225/yr when it saves **$2,625/yr** — and may skip the move on
> that basis. run `franchise.tax.delaware` with your own Schedule L figure
> before you weigh the $214 amendment fee against it.

⚠️ the $175 row genuinely is flat: the Authorized Shares Method does not read
gross assets at all, so no assets figure raises it.

see: `howto.reduce-franchise-tax-for-delaware-corp-solofounder.md`

### steps to reduce

1. draft board resolution
2. file Certificate of Amendment — **$214.00** base, ⚠️ *varies with stock*
3. update stock ledger

⛔ **this step read `$50`.** the real fee is **$214.00** per Delaware's schedule
(revised 2026-08-01), and the schedule marks it `*VARIES BASED ON STOCK` — which
a share-count amendment always is. so **$214.00 is a floor, not a quote**.

⚠️ **that changes whether this step suits your timeline.** you save $225.00/yr
($400.00 − $175.00, both from `franchise.tax.delaware`), so at $214.00 the fee is
roughly a **full year** of that, not the three months the neighboring brief used
to claim. the move is still correct; the urgency is not.

