## set reminders

> 🚩 **this table held two rows — `Feb 1` and `Feb 15` — and no others, until
> a later pass.** it was wrong in **three** independent ways, and this is the one
> file in the route whose entire job is to make sure the void never recurs.

### ⛔ March 1 is not one deadline — it is TWO, under two sections

§ 510 voids the charter on **either** default, and the word is *"or"*:

> "... neglects or refuses **for 1 year** to pay the State any franchise tax or
> taxes ..., **or shall neglect or refuse to file a complete annual franchise tax
> report**, the charter of the corporation **shall be void** ..."
>
> — 8 Del. C. § 510, https://delcode.delaware.gov/title8/c005/index.html

so a corporation that pays every dollar and skips the **report** is voided all
the same. the report has its own section and its own date:

> "(a) **Annually on or before March 1**, every corporation now existing or
> hereafter incorporated under Chapter 1 of this title ... **shall make an annual
> franchise tax report to the Secretary of State**."
>
> — 8 Del. C. § 502(a)

⭐ **calendar them as two items, not one.** a single "taxes due" reminder that you
satisfy with a payment leaves the void trigger fully armed.

### 🚨 and March 1 is the WRONG DATE once your tax reaches $5,000

this is the defect with teeth. § 504(a) opens with the March 1 rule and then
**replaces it** for larger taxpayers:

> "(a) The franchise tax shall be due and payable on **March 1** following the
> close of the calendar year, **except that** with respect to a corporation whose
> franchise tax liability for the current calendar year is **estimated to be
> $5,000 or more**, a tentative return and tax shall be due and payable as
> follows:
>
> (1) **Forty percent** of the estimated tax on **June 1** of the current year;
>
> (2) **Twenty percent** of the estimated tax on **September 1** of the current
> year;
>
> (3) **Twenty percent** of the estimated tax on **December 1** of the current
> year; and
>
> (4) **The remainder** of the tax as finally determined together with the annual
> franchise tax report on **March 1** following the close of the calendar year."
>
> — 8 Del. C. § 504(a)

⛔ **a corporation over that line which calendars March 1 alone has already missed
three due dates before the reminder fires**, and each one accrues interest:

> "(c) If the tax of any corporation remains unpaid after the due dates
> established by this section, the tax shall bear **interest at the rate of
> 1½ percent for each month or portion thereof** until fully paid."
>
> — 8 Del. C. § 504(c)

⚠️ **a transcription note, because it will bite whoever checks this.** the
plain-text rendering of the code prints `1½` as **`11/2`**. the rate is **one and
one-half percent per month**, compounded by no one — read it as **1.5%**, and do
not read `11/2` as eleven-halves or as a date.

⚠️ **and the $5,000 line is far lower than it sounds.** it is a **tax** figure,
not a revenue figure — the Authorized Shares Method reaches it on share count
alone, and a charter with millions of authorized shares can be billed many times
over it. **run `franchise.tax.delaware` before you assume you are under it.**

⭐ **§ 504(e) tells you what the estimate is built on:** *"The tentative return
and tax paid thereon under subsection (a) of this section shall be based on the
**annual franchise tax of the preceding year**."* so the year right after a
reinstatement is exactly when this bites — the preceding year is the one you just
settled.

### the table, corrected

| date | reminder | § |
|------|----------|---|
| **Jun 1** | ⚠️ **40% tentative payment** — only if estimated tax ≥ $5,000 | § 504(a)(1) |
| **Sep 1** | ⚠️ **20% tentative payment** — same condition | § 504(a)(2) |
| **Dec 1** | ⚠️ **20% tentative payment** — same condition | § 504(a)(3) |
| **Feb 1** | file the **annual report** *and* compute the balance | § 502(a) |
| **Feb 15** | final reminder — file and pay now | — |
| **Mar 1** | ⛔ **both** the report and the remaining tax are due | §§ 502(a), 504(a)(4) |
| **your agent's renewal date** | the registered agent fee — see the § 502(d) hazard below | § 502(d) |

🎯 **set the three tentative dates even if you are under the threshold today.** a
share amendment, an asset year, or a reinstatement can put you over it with no
notice at all, and a dormant calendar entry costs you no effort.

### ⚠️ do not let the registered agent lapse — § 502(d)

> "In case any corporation shall fail to file its annual franchise tax report and
> the franchise tax due ..., **and in case** the agent in charge of the registered
> office ... shall die, resign, **refuse to act as such**, remove from this State
> or cannot with due diligence be found, **it shall be lawful while default
> continues to serve process against the corporation upon the Secretary of
> State**."
>
> — 8 Del. C. § 502(d)

the two conditions are **cumulative**, so a paid-up agent shuts this door even
during a tax default. but an unpaid agent who declines to act reopens it — and
service on the State is service you will not hear about until a judgment exists.

add all of these to your calendar now.

